==English==

===Etymology===
Onomatopoeic.[[Category:English onomoatpoeias]] Compare Japanese {{term|フワフワ||lightly, softly|tr=fuwafuwa|lang=ja}}, Hungarian {{term|puha|lang=hu}} (“soft, fluffy”).
 
===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/flʌf/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/flVf/}}
* {{rhymes|ʌf}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Anything [[light]], [[soft]] or [[fuzzy]], especially [[fur]], [[hair]], [[feather]]s.
# Anything [[inconsequential]] or [[superficial]].
#: ''That article was basically a bunch of '''fluff'''. It didn't say anything substantive.''
# [[lapse|Lapse]], especially a [[mistake]] in an [[actor]]’s [[line]]s.
# A [[passive]] partner in a [[lesbian]] relationship.
{{rfex}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|anything light, soft or fuzzy}} [[fuzz]], [[puff]]
* {{sense|anything inconsequential or superficial}} [[BS]], [[cruft]], [[hype]], [[all talk]]
* {{sense|a lapse}} [[blooper]], [[blunder]], [[boo-boo]], [[defect]], [[error]], [[fault]], [[faux pas]], [[gaffe]], [[lapse]], [[mistake]], [[slip]], [[stumble]], [[thinko]]
* {{sense|passive in a lesbian relationship}} [[ruffle]]
* See also [[Wikisaurus:error]]

